# What NOT to ship to the Docker daemon when building the image.
#
# The build context is the repo ROOT (infra/docker-compose.yml sets `context: ..`), and without
# this file `COPY . .` sent every byte under it on EVERY build — measured at 3.7 GB of repo before
# counting anything the operator had put there. On a Docker Desktop host that transfer crosses a VM
# boundary, so it was minutes of waiting before the first command in the image even ran.
#
# The big one is not obvious: `crcon-db-data` is the folder the import runbook tells you to paste a
# multi-gigabyte CRCON backup into, and it lives at the repo root — inside the context. It reached
# the daemon on every rebuild despite the image having no use for it (the container reads it as a
# read-only bind mount at RUN time, never at BUILD time).
#
# Everything listed here is either regenerated inside the image or irrelevant to it.

# Dependencies + build caches — reinstalled and rebuilt in the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Build outputs — `pnpm build` produces these inside the image; a host copy would only shadow them.
**/dist
# The compiler's incremental record of a build on THIS machine. Copied in without the dist/ it
# describes, `tsc -b` reads it as up to date, emits nothing, and every dependent package then fails
# with "Cannot find module '@app/…'" — on any checkout that has ever been built outside Docker.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/panel/.next
apps/panel/out

# The operator's pasted CRCON backup (see docs/crcon-db-import.md). Bind-mounted at run time,
# never built into anything, and the largest thing in the context by far.
crcon-db-data

# The app's OWN backups — full-backup archives and trim archives. The compose default
# (BACKUPS_DIR: ../backups, relative to infra/) puts this folder at the repo root, inside the
# context, and unlike crcon-db-data it GROWS BY ITSELF: every "Create full backup now" press and
# every trim adds an archive, so a healthy long-running install crept toward a multi-gigabyte
# context transfer on every rebuild — measured at 4 GB on a live install — for a folder the
# build never reads (it is a run-time bind mount, exactly like the CRCON seed above).
backups

# Source control and local noise.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
*.log
.DS_Store

# Secrets must never reach an image layer — infra/.env holds live RCON and database passwords.
# (Compose passes it with --env-file at run time; the build has no business seeing it.)
infra/.env
**/.env
!infra/.env.example

# Installed plugins: bind-mounted into the api container at run time (installed-plugins/README.md),
# never built into the image.
installed-plugins
